The first measurements exposed an important G9 problem: with fully hidden affine parameters, the genuinely compact recovery still took thousands of modular operations. I’m tightening the formulation instead of rounding that number down. The affine frame will be instance data, while the witness remains the paper’s \((\omega,\gamma,\pi)\); at \(q=3001\) the honest structure-aware language still has about 1.8 million candidates, the reference scan is mechanical, and the multiplicative-coset recovery is actually under the 300-operation cap.
