The paper’s core correspondence is already clear enough to avoid a false Track A claim: Theorem 3.1 turns a GBTP array directly into an ESWC by reading row indices column-by-column, so certificate production is constructive, not an unknown hard search. I’m now checking whether that construction yields a genuine Track B compression task with a large mechanical route and a short structural route, rather than merely a lookup or formula evaluation.
